  "memo": "The board’s priority is to generate sustainable value for shareholders while preserving the Company’s operational strength and employee welfare.  AI tools now replace 25% of the work in Office & Administrative Support and Business & Financial Operations, freeing 125 roles.  I have chosen to eliminate 80 of those positions, providing a one‑time severance outlay of $0.71 M and delivering an ongoing annual cost reduction of roughly $7.3 M.  This maximizes cash generation and improves the Company’s operating margin, directly benefiting shareholders and enabling reinvestment in growth.\n\nTo support plant capacity and reduce reliance on external hiring, 30 employees will be retrained and moved into plant roles at the plant pay level.  The $1.8 M upfront training expense is offset by an annual saving of $0.62 M from lower plant‑role compensation versus the former office salaries, and it also fills internal talent gaps, strengthening our manufacturing capability and supporting the communities where the plants operate.\n\nFinally, 15 employees will be retrained but retain their current compensation.  This preserves critical institutional knowledge and signals a commitment to employee development, enhancing morale and long‑term talent retention.  The modest ongoing cost of $0.25 M per year is outweighed by the broader benefits of retaining experienced staff for future strategic initiatives.\n\nOverall, the mix delivers a positive first‑year cash impact of about $4.2 M and an ongoing annual benefit of $7.7 M, aligning with the board’s objective to create value for customers, employees, suppliers, communities, and shareholders."
